# R9 raw fetched data: netztransparenz.de publishes NO explicit reuse licence
# for the reBAP (statutory norms apply), so the raw reBAP series must not be
# redistributed via git. intraday_prices.csv holds it (plus the aWattar
# day-ahead, itself already ignored above), so it stays local and regenerable.
intraday_prices.csv
intraday_meta.json
intraday_analysis.png
wc_intraday.png

# Intentionally tracked result JSONs (the pages read them in the browser):
#   wc_load_results.json, wc_permutation_results.json  -> worldcup.html
#   forecast_value.json, event_study_results.json      -> index.html (one-pager)

# NOTE: these are intentionally NOT ignored and should be committed:
#   results.json          demo page data, refreshed daily by the workflow
#   wc_results.json       World Cup study output, read by worldcup.html
#   wc_matches.csv        the (user-edited) match schedule
#   intraday_results.json R9 output read by intraday.html. AGGREGATES ONLY
#     (median spreads by hour, volatility ratios, overlap counts), derived from
#     reBAP; it does NOT contain the raw reBAP series, so committing it is not a
#     redistribution of the netztransparenz dataset.
#   wc_intraday_results.json R3 output. Same reasoning: per-match-day median
#     deltas and permutation aggregates derived from the reBAP, never the series.

forecast_ladder_days.png
forecast_ladder_residuals.png

.DS_Store
.tokensave
.claude
